  Liquid OS advancements update: the Wednesday release note is staged and still
  hidden, but the seven-day buildout is materially bigger than a short teaser.

  Current highlights in the 2026-06-03 draft:
  - Project Health Monitor now has Notion Health write-back v0.1, an hourly
  refresh pipeline with honest staleness reporting, and a COO morning brief that
  summarizes project verdicts and items needing attention.
  - Onboarding tracker is much easier to operate: search, filters, sortable
  columns, sticky headers, and clearer links.
  - People surfaces now show employment type and hire type in more places, future
  hires show as Pre-hire instead of Terminated, and email copy controls are
  available across directory, profile, and tracker rows.
  - Liquid Slack Bot can answer against company-history material, walk org
  subtrees without stalling, and filter people searches by employment type and
  hire type.
  - Liquid Companion has daily auto-summary back at the user-set time, approved
  summaries syncing to the web app, Local (LFM) / Cloud (Anthropic) backend
  selection, and updated local model support.
  - Model Adoption added per-section CSV export and chart-axis fixes for single-
  value histories.
  - Offboarding tracker and overview are live as a limited rollout for the
  offboarding and finance group, with broader access still gated.
  - Foundations also moved: Notion-owned project fields are protected from
  accidental overwrites, shared UI primitives were extracted, and test coverage
  landed around several cron, dashboard, onboarding, and helper paths.

  The release note is not public yet. Final step is the Wednesday publish flip,
  production /release-notes smoke, then the channel announcement.
